    "# 2. Implement an n-gram extractor <font color=\"#2680EB\">[5%]</font>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Implement the function `ngrams(text,size)`, which should produce all sub-sequences of `size` words present in the cleaned text. \n",
    "\n",
    "Note that `ngrams` is a list, and each element of that list is a *string*.\n",
    "\n",
    "The only words you must consider in a ngram are words having at least `MIN_TOKEN_LENGTH` characters.\n",
    "\n",
    "You can use the [split](https://docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#string.split) and [join](https://docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#string.join) function of the split library. Remember that to extract elements *i* to *j* of array *a* you use `a[i:j]`.\n",
    "\n",
    "<font size=\"-1\" color=\"gray\">(Remove this cell when delivering.)</font>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<font size=\"+1\" color=\"#2680EB\">**Implement the ngram extractor.**</font>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "MIN_TOKEN_LENGTH = 4\n",
    "\n",
    "def ngrams(text, size):\n",
    "    \n",
    "    text = clean(text)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # YOUR CODE HERE\n",
    "    words = [word for word in text.split() if len(word)>=MIN_TOKEN_LENGTH]\n",
    "\n",
    "    ngrams = []\n",
    "    start_idx = 0\n",
    "    while start_idx + size <= len(words):\n",
    "        ngrams.append(\" \".join(words[start_idx:start_idx+size]))\n",
    "        start_idx += 1\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return(ngrams)"
   ]
  },
